Z||000011||batboy||08-01-99||08:26 AM||||Now the angel has the advantage and the devil's worried. I had a bunch of bills roll in during the past two days that need to be paid. Since the V6 engine swap would be at least three times more expensive then the 2.5 replacement and I need my everyday car back soon and I don't have a lot of cash right now... well, it don't take a rocket scientist to figure this one out. **sigh** My little red horny friend is desperately trying to make a compromise with the halo wearing dude right now. Put a 2.5 back in the 87 SE right now and then buy another Fiero with a V6 and 5 speed, like maybe a cool 88 Formula, later on when "we" can afford it. That way I'd have an economical 4 cylinder daily commuter car, a sporty fun to drive V6 Fiero, and an awesome muscular V8 batmobile. Hmmmm, I'm being to really like this plan.
